Package: bicorX
Type: Package
Title: Robust Differential Co-Expression Analysis for Compositional and Multi-Omics Data
Authors@R: person("Payton", "Yau", email = "tungon@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Version: 0.0.1
Description: Robust differential co-expression analysis based on biweight
    midcorrelation, extending three previously-published, never-packaged
    methods for modern multi-omics and compositional data: BMHT (Zheng,
    Yuan, Sha & Sun (2014) <doi:10.1186/1471-2105-15-S15-S3>), ROS-DET
    (Kayano, Takigawa, Shiga, Tsuda & Mamitsuka (2011)
    <doi:10.1093/nar/gkr130>), and BMKC (Yuan, Zheng, Xia & Huang (2015)
    <doi:10.1155/2015/836929>). Includes explicit, documented departures
    from the original methods where scale or the compositional/multi-omics
    data regime required them (e.g. k-core decomposition in place of exact
    k-clique percolation for BMKC's module extraction; see NEWS.md and the
    package vignettes for a full per-method fidelity account) - this is not
    presented as a strictly faithful reimplementation of any of the three.
SystemRequirements: An optimized BLAS (e.g. OpenBLAS) is strongly
    recommended over R's default reference BLAS. Measured ~1.3-1.4x
    speedup on the correlation-matrix computation that dominates this
    package's runtime, at zero code changes - purely a matter of which
    BLAS library R is linked against. On Debian/Ubuntu:
    'sudo update-alternatives --config libblas.so.3-x86_64-linux-gnu'
    after installing 'libopenblas0-pthread' (or '-serial'/'-openmp'
    depending on your threading needs). Check your current BLAS with
    'sessionInfo()'.
